From d17316001e91d69e22514559b6bfa29e3328ea07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cline <cline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 01:34:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(squad-share): make daily.dev Squad posting actually work

The workflow failed on every real post with "curl: (3) URL rejected: Malformed
input to a URL function" because SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL was never set, and it passed
silently on pushes that only updated a post, so the failure was easy to miss.

- Fail fast with an explicit ::error:: naming the missing secret.
- Derive the post slug the way Astro does (src/utils/post-slug.mjs) instead of
  from the raw filename, which produced 404 links for Simple-Ghostty-... and
  "update-tpm- ...(1).md".
- Fix the double-encoded mojibake in the message (rocket + em dash).
- Build the Slack payload with jq --arg so a title containing quotes cannot
  break it.
- Trim CRLF frontmatter so the one CRLF post keeps a clean title.
- Pass the changed-file list through the environment instead of interpolating
  it into the shell, and use LF line endings like the other workflows.

Verified by dry-running the extracted step against all 32 posts: 32 valid
payloads, and every URL matches postSlug().
